{"benchmark": "ifeval", "task_id": "1092", "sample_idx": 22, "model_name": "google/gemma-3n-e4b-it", "content": "## Lost (and Found) in Japan\n\nJapan. The word itself conjures images of ancient temples, bustling cities, and serene gardens. And let me tell you, it delivers on all fronts! I just returned from a whirlwind trip and I'm still processing the incredible experience.\n\nMy journey started in Tokyo, a sensory overload in the best way possible. Neon lights, incredible food stalls (ramen, sushi, takoyaki – I tried it all!), and a palpable energy filled every corner. I explored the vibrant Shibuya crossing, found peace in the Meiji Jingu Shrine, and got delightfully lost in the electric town of Akihabara.\n\nNext, I took the Shinkansen (bullet train!) to Kyoto. The contrast was stunning. Here, history reigned supreme. I wandered through the breathtaking Fushimi Inari Shrine with its thousands of red torii gates, marvelled at the Golden Pavilion (Kinkaku-ji), and strolled through the enchanting Arashiyama Bamboo Grove.\n\nBeyond the sights, it was the culture that truly captivated me. The politeness, the respect, the attention to detail – it’s all so deeply ingrained. I learned a few basic Japanese phrases (arigato goes a long way!) and embraced the ritual of bowing.\n\nJapan is a country of contrasts, a place where ancient traditions seamlessly blend with modern innovation. It's a feast for the senses and a balm for the soul. I left feeling inspired, refreshed, and already dreaming of my return. Highly recommend adding it to your travel list!\n", "logprobs": [{"token": "##", "logprob": -1.4305104514278355e-06}, {"token": "▁Lost", "logprob": -0.0011843579122796655}, {"token": "▁(", "logprob": -0.16028544306755066}, {"token": "and", "logprob": -1.0728830375228426e-06}, {"token": "▁Found", "logprob": -0.0015997005393728614}, {"token": ")", "logprob": -0.15122127532958984}, {"token": "▁in", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": "▁Japan", "logprob": -0.0901465117931366}, {"tok